# Pairs with ClaimHeadCoversPriorAppends. The claim head is read when the entry is
# written, not under the lock that raises the in-memory entry. An append the
# superseded activation makes between the write and the raise lies above the
# head the raised activation replays to.
MODULE: ClaimHeadCoversPriorAppendsHeadAtWrite
TARGET: ClaimHeadCoversPriorAppends
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the claim head is read at the entry write instead of at the raise
PERTURBS: ClaimWrite, ClaimRaise

--- FIND
    /\ fence' = Max2(fence, epoch[a])
    /\ cstage' = [cstage EXCEPT ![a] = 2]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<rowEpoch, rowInc, up, seen, seenInc, epoch, claimHead, prior, dupUsed>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ fence' = Max2(fence, epoch[a])
    /\ cstage' = [cstage EXCEPT ![a] = 2]
\* MUTATION: the head is read with the entry write.
    /\ claimHead' = [claimHead EXCEPT ![a] = next]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<rowEpoch, rowInc, up, seen, seenInc, epoch, prior, dupUsed>>
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ claimHead' = [claimHead EXCEPT ![a] = next]
    /\ prior'
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the raise returns the head the write read.
    /\ UNCHANGED claimHead
    /\ prior'
--- END
